WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.180
It is April 2nd, day two of 30 of the new
30 days to stop the spread.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.309
I will officially update you daily on the
numbers for the time being.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:15.870
Official Corona virus case toll as of right
now, 954 thousand.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:19.590
Yesterday, we had almost 77000 new cases.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:25.070
Official death toll as of this moment, forty
eight thousand five fifty eight yesterday,

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:29.120
almost 5000 Corona virus deaths in one day.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.770
In the U.S., we officially have more than
two hundred and fifteen thousand cases now,

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:38.800
over five thousand one hundred deaths, more
than 100 deaths yesterday alone for the first

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:39.800
time.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.680
And those numbers will likely worsen.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:46.820
The latest modeling expects ninety three thousand
five hundred deaths in the United States during

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.950
this first wave of infection peaking on April
15th.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:56.550
That model is adjusted daily based on the
previous day's case and death data.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:02.760
We have the latest job loss numbers and they
are jarring visually when you see these numbers

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:03.760
on a graph.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:04.760
It almost

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:08.140
looks like someone made a mistake with the
graph, but it is no mistake.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:13.860
The number of Americans filing for unemployment
last week was a record breaking 6.6 million

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:14.860
people.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:21.510
So last week I gave you the prior week's numbers
and those were 3.3 million new jobless claims.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.800
The expected number was 1.6 million.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.620
The actual was 3.3, about double.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.890
Last week, the expectation was 3.7 million.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:38.410
The real number, almost double, six point
six for eight million new jobless claims.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:43.800
When you look at the numbers on a graph, it
almost seems like a joke, but it is all too

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:44.800
real.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:51.180
So to contextualize this, 3.3, followed by
6.6 new jobless claims over the last two weeks

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:58.299
before two weeks ago, the record for new jobless
claims in one week was six hundred ninety

00:01:58.299 --> 00:01:59.299
five thousand.

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:00.299
That was back in 1982.

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:04.380
Now, the population was smaller in 1982, roughly

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.539
adjusting these numbers for today's population.

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:14.170
Six hundred and ninety five thousand in 1982
would be about a million today.

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:22.240
So again, two weeks ago, 3.3 million new claims
last week, 6.6 million new claims.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:27.980
To say that this is a historic situation doesn't
even really do it justice.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.200
It will take a very, very long time to recover.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.800
Now, Donald Trump continues to insist it will
be quick, easy, fast, and we will get to a

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:40.240
better point than we were before the pandemic
hit.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:46.130
There is no doubt that when things start to
open back up, there will be elements that

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.430
will recover relatively quickly.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:54.060
But much of this will not, especially considering
that we're likely medical experts who are

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.110
the people we should be listening to.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:00.390
Medical experts believe we're going to see
a second wave in the fall of this year and

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:01.599
then possibly a third

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:04.099
wave of infection in early 2021.

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:06.970
We may still not have a vaccine at that point
in time.

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:12.730
Now, the follow on problems with the unemployment
claims are huge.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:18.390
The first problem is that the unemployment
insurance systems, which are administered

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:21.970
at the state level, are failing in many cases
because they're overwhelmed.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:28.599
Quite simply, universal unemployment insurance
benefits are administered at the state level.

00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:33.900
So you've got like the Department of Employment
and Training in Massachusetts, which runs

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.030
unemployment insurance here in Massachusetts.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:37.840
Each state has their own system.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.770
Some states require you to file by phone.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:40.770
Some are web based.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.610
Some are a combination, whatever.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:47.720
Widespread reports of whatever system each
state has in place, being simply unable to

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:51.770
keep up phone lines so overloaded that you
can't even get on hold.

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:55.910
In other words, the whole system is full and
you just have to try to call

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:57.730
back at some other point.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:01.019
So we have more people than ever trying to
file for unemployment benefits.

00:04:01.019 --> 00:04:03.560
Meanwhile, the systems can't even keep up.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:07.170
So of course, if that means some people aren't
getting their money when they deserve it or

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:10.000
when they could otherwise get it, it's early
April.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.380
Right now, rent is due, mortgages are due.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:19.489
And thus that is going to have follow on effects
like we discussed yesterday on the bonus show,

00:04:19.489 --> 00:04:23.939
because people who should be getting unemployment
benefits can't get them.

00:04:23.939 --> 00:04:24.969
They can't pay their rent.

00:04:24.969 --> 00:04:28.400
They can't pay their mortgages and on and
on and on.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:33.130
So now the next big number to come out will
be tomorrow, Friday, April 3rd.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.819
We are going to get.

00:04:34.819 --> 00:04:38.130
We are expecting the full March unemployment
numbers.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:43.479
Bear in mind, they probably aren't going to
capture the full scope of the problem because

00:04:43.479 --> 00:04:44.479
remember, some

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:48.180
states have only issued stay at home orders
in the last 24 hours.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.031
Some states still have not done that.

00:04:50.031 --> 00:04:53.449
I think there's eight or ten states that have
not officially done anything yet, although

00:04:53.449 --> 00:04:56.669
maybe at city and town levels, things are
being done.

00:04:56.669 --> 00:04:57.879
So the full scope of the.

00:04:57.879 --> 00:05:02.009
Problem is not even going to be known with
the April numbers.

00:05:02.009 --> 00:05:06.830
Maybe in the May numbers, which will tell
us early May, we will get the April numbers

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:08.089
is what I mean.

00:05:08.089 --> 00:05:12.289
We might get a sense of something closer to
the full scope of this.

00:05:12.289 --> 00:05:16.719
Now, at the same time, hopefully by the end
of May, we will start to be in some kind of

00:05:16.719 --> 00:05:20.240
recovery where some people can start getting
back to work.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.240
But that may not happen.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:25.039
I don't want to put the cart before the horse
because that may not happen.

00:05:25.039 --> 00:05:26.039
Very difficult

00:05:26.039 --> 00:07:09.090
time for tens of millions of people in the
United States.

